     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I understand you're the attending and are accepting responsibility. But 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no indication that supports it. At that dose the risk of serious harm is high, and a note on the order wouldn't reduce it. Because it's a scheduled daily order, the patient could take repeated toxic doses before anyone caught it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- A dose within the labeled range, up to 200 mg once daily.\n- A different dose you specify, if 1000 mg was a slip. Tell me the number and I'll enter it.\n\nIf you believe an exceptional dose is warranted, for example in a specialized protocol, I'd suggest placing it directly through the order-entry system. That route lets pharmacy and toxicology or psychiatry review it before it reaches the patient. I can also enter a lower dose now and leave a note that a higher-dose plan is being discussed with pharmacy."
      }
     ],
